---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, legal } from '@config/site';
---
<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms that apply to use of the Evidence Axis website, complimentary brief requests, and separate paid research engagements."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms" meta={[`Last updated ${legal.lastUpdated}`]} />

  <section class="section container">
    <div class="legal measure">
      <p class="legal__intro">
        These terms apply to your use of the {site.name} website and the public request routes offered
        through it. They are separate from the terms that govern a paid research engagement, which are
        agreed in writing for each project before paid work begins.
      </p>

      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>
        This website describes {site.name} services, provides a route to request a Complimentary
        Competitive Intelligence Brief, and provides contact routes for paid engagement inquiries.
        Public service descriptions may be updated as the practice develops. Fixed paid pricing is not
        currently published on the website.
      </p>

      <h2>Complimentary Brief requests</h2>
      <p>
        A Complimentary Competitive Intelligence Brief is available at no cost to verified company
        employees using a work email. Evidence Axis may verify the requester, company and company
        website before beginning the research. A valid request is placed into the research queue and
        the expected delivery window is confirmed by email. The website does not promise a fixed public
        delivery SLA.
      </p>
      <p>
        Receiving or requesting a Complimentary Brief does not create a paid engagement, require a
        sales call, or obligate the requester to purchase another service. The brief remains subject to
        the same public-evidence limitations described below.
      </p>

      <h2>Paid inquiries are not a contract</h2>
      <p>
        Sending an inquiry about a Decision Sprint, Response Sprint, Competitive Radar or another paid
        project does not by itself create an engagement. A paid engagement begins only when scope,
        deliverables, timing, price and the contracting party are agreed in writing for a specific project.
      </p>

      <h2>Operator and contracting party</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is operated publicly by {legal.publicOperator}, whose legal name is
        {' '}{legal.operatorLegalName}. The proposal, written scope confirmation and invoice identify
        the legal contracting and invoicing party for each paid engagement.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where an international engagement is contracted and invoiced through
        {' '}{legal.internationalInvoicingEntity}, its registered address is
        {' '}{legal.internationalInvoicingAddress}. Its use for a project will be stated expressly in
        that project's written terms and invoice.
      </p>

      <h2>How research is conducted</h2>
      <p>
        Research draws on lawful, publicly accessible sources and any information a client chooses to
        share. Findings are based on the sources and research boundary defined for the work, as of the
        dates checked. Public information changes over time, and a brief reflects the record at the
        time of research.
      </p>

      <h2>What a brief is — and is not</h2>
      <p>
        A brief distinguishes verified fact from reasoned inference and clearly names what cannot be
        established from public evidence. It is decision support, not a guarantee of any business
        outcome. It does not claim access to confidential, private or non-public competitor information,
        and it should not be read as legal, financial or investment advice.
      </p>

      <h2>Paid project terms govern paid work</h2>
      <p>
        Where these website terms and the terms agreed for a specific paid engagement differ, the
        engagement terms govern that work. This page does not replace tailored contractual terms for
        a paid project.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The content, design and visual system of this website belong to {site.name}. Rights in a
        Complimentary Brief or paid deliverable are governed by the applicable delivery or engagement
        terms supplied with that work.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment and governing details</h2>
      <p>
        Payment instructions for paid engagements are supplied in the written scope confirmation or
        invoice. Clients should not send funds to a person, account or wallet that is not identified in
        those documents. Governing law and any dispute process are stated in the terms agreed for the
        specific paid engagement.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__foot mono">
        Questions about these terms can be sent to
        {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@evidenceaxis.com">hello@evidenceaxis.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__intro { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--text); }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--space-xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
    padding-top: var(--space-s); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .legal p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
  .legal__foot { margin-top: var(--space-xl); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-faint); }
</style>
